 "result": "maze.py is a flat-grid BFS. It pads the input into a bytearray with a '#' border, marks visited cells by overwriting them with '#', and expands frontier by level, printing the distance when it reaches E or -1 if the frontier empties. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78). The assay was accepted with baseline median 3.42688 and noise 3.9%. I did not run a timing test on a 1000x1000 maze, and I did not attempt a faster variant, so further gains are unexplored. Resting to keep the verified body and pass unspent energy to the colony.",
